<title>USA: Continental Homes reinstitutes buyback.</title>
<headline>Continental Homes reinstitutes buyback.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Homes Holding Corp said Friday it has reinstituted a stock repurchase plan previously approved by its board.</p>
<p>The buyback originally instituted in December 1994 authorized the repurchase of 500,000 shares of its Continental Homes common stock, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said it is reinstituting the buyback because it believes its stock is undervalued. The stock was trading at 16-3/8 Friday afternoon, up 1/8. Its 52-week low is 16.</p>
